  "title": "Operating Systems",
  "description": "What an operating system is and how it runs the machine underneath your programs. Chapter 1 takes the grand tour from Operating System Concepts: what an OS does, how a computer boots, interrupts and DMA, the storage hierarchy and caching, multiprocessors and clusters, multiprogramming and timesharing, dual-mode operation and the timer, process, memory, storage and I/O management, protection and security, the data structures inside a kernel, and computing environments from phones to the cloud. Every short reading is followed by a quiz (multiple choice, true or false, and typed answers), with drills, Python exercises that build a tiny dual-mode machine and kernel data structures, and a review to close each part.",
